 34S  c  1985Al03,1986Al21: {+34}S(n,n),(n,n') with 21.7 and 25.5-MeV           
 34S 2c  monoenergetic neutrons produced via the 3H(d,n)4He reaction using a    
 34S 3c  pulsed and bunched deuteron beam at the Ohio University Beam Swinger   
 34S 4c  time-of-flight facility. The targets were 93.6% and 94.5%-enriched     
 34S 5c  {+34}S powder. Scattered neutrons were detected utilizing a seven-fold 
 34S 6c  array of NE213 liquid scintillation detectors. Measured |s(E{-n},|q).  
 34S 7c  1985Al03 deduced proton ($M_p$) and neutron ($M_n$) multipole matrix   
 34S 8c  elements for E2 transitions to the first three 2+ states in 34S using  
 34S 9c  coupled-channels (CC) analysis. 1986Al21 deduced Isoscalar E2, E3, and 
 34S Ac  E4 reduced transition matrix elements using the anharmonic vibrational 
 34S Bc  (AHV) collective model within a coupled-channels framework.            
